<article class="env-lemma" id="06UB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06UB">Lemma <span data-tag="06UB">101.23.3</span>.</a> A base change of a locally quasi-finite morphism is locally quasi-finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have seen this for quasi-DM morphisms in Lemma <a href="/tag/050F" data-tag="050F">101.4.4</a> and for locally finite type morphisms in Lemma <a href="/tag/06FU" data-tag="06FU">101.17.3</a>. It is immediate that the condition on fibres is inherited by a base change. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>